# User wording does not waive merge gates

These phrases do **not** waive applicable required CI, `bot-feedback-gate`, or thread closure in **`WORKFLOW.md`** / **`git-pr-workflow-default.mdc`**:

- "Merge everything" / "batch merge" / "land the queue"
- "Just merge" / "urgency" / frustration tone
- "CI green" / "checks passed" while threads are missing or unsettled
- Skipping `bot-feedback-gate` or substantive feedback disposition/resolution

Reviewer vendors, Qwen, and reviewer-presence checks remain advisory. Agents use single-shot audits and park while only GitHub-owned work is pending; they do not create wait cycles or use `--watch` loops. Only an explicit written waiver for that specific PR waives feedback closeout for that PR.

Full ship bar: **`WORKFLOW.md`** (repo root). Cursor summary: **`git-pr-workflow-default.mdc`**.
